.TH DTCREGDUMP 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
DTCRegDump \- print a formatted dump of a DTC's registers and counters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B DTCRegDump
.RB [ \-d
.IR dtc ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-R ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-e ]
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B DTCRegDump
constructs a
.B DTCLib::DTC_Registers
object with
.B skipInit
set, so it reads the card without reconfiguring it.
It first prints
.BR "Terminal is \fIC\fPx\fIL\fP" ,
then
.BR "Driver Version: \fIstring\fP"
(from
.BR M_IOC_GET_VERSION ),
then the register dump: one
.B RegisterFormatter
block per register with address, raw value, name and decoded fields.
Width follows the terminal (capped at 120 columns when wider than 400).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " dtc"
Card index
.RI ( /dev/mu2e N ).
Default:
.B DTCLIB_DTC
if set, else 0.
.TP
.BI \-m " file"
Simulator memory file (default
.IR mu2esim.bin );
used only in simulation mode.
.TP
.B \-R
Do not print the register dump.
.TP
.B \-p
Print the performance counters.
.TP
.B \-e
Print the SERDES error counters.
.TP
.B \-c
Print the Mu2e protocol packet counters.
.TP
.B \-s
Prints
.B "NOT IMPLEMENTED"
(SERDES byte/packet counters were removed).
.TP
.B \-h
Usage, exit 0.
An unknown option prints
.B "Unknown option"
and the usage, and exits 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success.
If the node cannot be opened the library throws and the process aborts
(status 134).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DTCLIB_DTC
Default card index.
.TP
.B DTCLIB_SIM_ENABLE
If set, overrides the requested hardware mode in the
.B DTC_Registers
constructor; any value that maps to a simulator mode (e.g.
.BR 1 ,
which
.B Setup_DTC.sh
exports on hosts whose name lacks \(dqmu2edaq\(dq) makes this tool dump the
software simulator instead of the card.
.SH FILES
.BI /dev/mu2e N
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
DTCRegDump \-d 1 | grep \-A1 \(aqFPGA Temperature\(aq
DTCRegDump \-R \-e \-c
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR my_cntl (1),
.BR CFORegDump (1),
.BR dtcPrometheusExporter (1),
.BR mu2e (4),
.BR libDTCInterface (3)
